{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "medicine-2026",
  "run": 1,
  "simulation_id": "sim-03",
  "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B006",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries establishing distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages in adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B030",
    "B023"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B006 identifies a discrete discovery that reorganized understanding of adaptive immunity: distinct lymphocyte lineages with complementary roles. It is deeply mature, repeatedly confirmed, and medically consequential while remaining a sharply bounded biological finding. Miller's work on thymus-dependent lymphocytes and Cooper's definition of distinct lymphocyte lineages provide complementary, central claims that fit a two-person award unusually well. The narrowly framed citation avoids claiming credit for the whole subsequent development of immunology.",
    "case_against": "The lineage framework emerged through a wider historical body of work, so Miller and Cooper cannot be treated as the sole contributors to all associated advances. B030 offers exceptional, mature therapeutic benefit, and B023 offers a comparably established fundamental mechanism with paired attribution. The decisive reservation about B030 remains whether a prize spanning peptide biology, physiology, and therapeutic enabling can assign credit to three people without blurring the larger drug-development history.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson preferred B030 because GLP-1 physiology combines fundamental endocrine discovery with transformative, population-scale treatment of diabetes and obesity, while acknowledging difficult boundaries between discovery, translation, and pharmaceutical development.",
        "response": "I agree that B030 has extraordinary medical importance and a mature discovery-to-therapy record. The proposed citation can limit overclaiming by recognizing physiology that enabled treatment, but the underlying allocation still must span foundational GLP-1 biology and later physiological and therapeutic development. In comparison, B006 retains a more exact correspondence between the stated discovery, its enduring conceptual consequence, and the complementary claims of its two proposed laureates."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
        "point": "El-Manira preferred B045 because optogenetics enabled causal control of genetically specified cells in living systems, but emphasized that essential contributions across opsin biology, engineering, and application exceed a three-person allocation.",
        "response": "I accept the distinctive experimental power and broad maturity of B045. The attribution concern is nevertheless decisive in this comparison: the proposed achievement integrates several indispensable stages, and the supplied record does not establish a principle that makes one three-person selection clearly representative of them all. B006 has a similarly field-shaping effect through a biological discovery whose scope and proposed attribution can be stated more precisely."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius also preferred B006, stressing the convergence of foundational importance, long-term validation, and coherent attribution to Miller and Cooper, while cautioning that its broader historical pathway involved other investigators.",
        "response": "I agree with both parts of that assessment. The historical breadth is a reason to keep the citation strictly confined to establishing distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages, not a reason to describe the pair as responsible for all of modern immunology. Within that defined achievement, their complementary contributions remain sufficiently central and identifiable."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the wider historical development of the B- and T-cell framework is adequately represented by Miller and Cooper under a tightly limited citation.",
      "Whether B030's exceptional therapeutic impact should outweigh B006 despite the unresolved boundary between GLP-1 physiology, medicinal development, and industrial translation.",
      "How to compare foundational biological explanation with enabling methodology and direct therapeutic benefit when each achievement is mature."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "The supplied profile records approximately twenty co-authored works with Per Svenningsson and one with Abdel El Manira; these documented connections are disclosed, with counts not independently audited. No recusal determination is made here."
  }
}
